# Energy-Efficient TSPC Flip-Flop Design

This project presents an optimized True Single Phase Clocked (TSPC) flip-flop architecture for high-performance, low-power VLSI systems. The design integrates input-aware pre-charge, floating-node analysis, SET/RESET functionality, and SEU-tolerant improvements. Implemented using Tanner EDA (S-Edit & T-Spice), the proposed flip-flop achieves up to **80% power reduction** and **26% delay improvement** compared to the traditional TGFF, making it ideal for modern low-voltage, high-speed digital circuits.

## 🚀 Features
- Optimized TSPC architecture for reduced power and delay  
- Input-aware pre-charge mechanism  
- Floating-node stability analysis  
- Integrated SET/RESET operation  
- SEU-tolerant design modifications  
- Tanner EDA simulation results with waveform analysis  

## 🛠 Tools & Technologies
- **Tanner EDA Suite** (S-Edit, T-Spice)  
- **CMOS VLSI Design**  
- **Low-Power Digital Design**  
- **Power & Delay Analysis**  

